<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kollidam River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Coleroon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kollidam, also called the Coleroon, is the northern distributary of the Kaveri river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It branches off just above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srirangam">Srirangam</a>, enclosing the island temple town between its two streams, and flows north-east to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>. It has long marked the northern edge of the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> delta, separating it from the lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gingee">Gingee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcot">Arcot</a> regions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kollidam-river.jpg" alt="Kollidam River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arivazhakan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kollidam_River.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
